# TEST_MODE : MULTI_MODULE_OK

# ComPtr( of T ) across SEPARATELY COMPILED modules.
#
# Instantiations are module-private -- there is no working COMDAT on PE/COFF by
# either route tried, so each module keeps its own copy of ComPtr( of IFake )
# and its members. That costs size, not correctness, and this test is what
# says so: both modules instantiate the same type, the link succeeds without a
# duplicate-symbol error, and a reference DETACHED in one module is ATTACHED
# and released in the other with the count intact.
#
# The private helpers in comptr.bi -- hAsUnk, hIidUnknown, hCanonical -- are
# the other half of the claim. A header that defined them non-privately would
# fail to link here, which is the reason they are private.

MAIN := comptr-mm-main.bas
SRCS := comptr-mm-b.bas
